WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
But they're printing now a collection of essays on education, and this is one of the essays that they took from this article.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:27.000
And basically, how harmful was this myth of saying everybody in the other country was a superman, and you are a dum-dum.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:40.000
And therefore instilled in the student the whole feeling that he's never going to understand them.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:51.000
And this created a horrible, horrible psychological aura for the student in the sense that,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:59.000
well, if I'm never going to be able to study, if my grandmother will shut me out there,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:09.000
and I can hardly read the letters, and I went to college or whatever it is, or I went to high school, I know algebra, I know this,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:18.000
then why should I study? And I am very, very strong against that type of thing.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Even if it would be true, we should not say it. Of course you can when it's not true.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:34.000
But this idea, I mean, for instance, even a great man like Louis Gibbsburg, Louis Gibbsburg was a great scholar,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.000
if you know anything about this, he was one of the greatest scholars of the century,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
and he believed that there is no purpose in teaching Torah to Americans. You cannot teach Torah to an American.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:56.000
An American Jew, no. Just like you're teaching Torah to a subhuman species.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:09.000
And it's very, they developed cynicism and so on, and it was very harmful, I think it was very harmful.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Well, the amnesia that goes on, trying to tell somebody that in the 1920s they had a full-time rabbi working for the elect,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Oh, I didn't know that.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Yeah. There were Jews being put to death up there, because Jews were into rackets and this and that, prostitution.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Yeah, the rolling point, yes, of course.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Well, even before that. But, you know, Jews were involved in these things.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:47.000
I mean, the Torah, when they brought up the Torah, I don't know, grandparents or parents were involved in illegal liquor drinking.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Yeah.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
Time period in my lab was, you know, yeah, and so.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Today, I believe that there is a lot of Torah in the world, but I would say, with no prejudice against anybody,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.000
to get the Torah in Israel, I don't see much learning of Torah in America.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:14.000
And, I think that the level of study in Israel is much, it's difficult to get it.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:22.000
The Tamir HaKamim, that the quality of the Tamir HaKamim that you have in Israel, you don't have it in America.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.000
It's a different quality.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.000
We had old people in America, like the Spanish came and others, but they were all, say, the Jewish Alamajim.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.000
But, when they died, yes, even the good Tamirim that they had, they moved to Israel.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Very interesting.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:46.000
We don't have, in America today, we don't have the great Tamir HaKamim.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.000
Even I'm talking, interesting.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:56.000
I once, I observed, I don't believe the Torah, I said, you know what?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.000
I said, well, what do we get?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.000
The Reform, the Conservative, and so on.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.000
I said, that's not true.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.000
Because, when one level of Judaism goes down, it affects all of us.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.000
And, that's the truth.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:19.000
And, there's this thing about, you know, homosexuality, lesbians, and rabbis, and performing same-sex marriage, and so on.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.000
It will affect all the other people.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:31.000
So, anyhow, one point that I wanted to make in this connection is that, even great Reform scholars, today, the Conservative movement is gone.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Intellectually, it's totally gone.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.000
It's a great loss to all of Judaism.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:44.000
Can you believe that, 10, 15 years ago, if you would ask any Jew, who knows anything, if you would ask James Salovey a Jew,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.000
who's the greatest communist in the world?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.000
He would say, probably, he would say, he would answer, he would say, Saul Lieberman.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
About this.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.000
Anybody, you know, who's the greatest philosopher, would say, Heschel.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Or, the greatest biblical scholar, would say, H. L. Ginsburg.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.000
But, today, they have nothing.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Totally gone.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.000
So, we should start now.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.000
We have a nice place.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:26.000
I remember hearing scholars, they had a thing in the early 70s.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Scholars would go around to different congregations to try to find homes.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.000
They called it scholar residence, and so on.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.000
Yeah.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.000
No scholars.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.000
No scholars.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:52.000
The truth is, that, I believe, the center of Judaism today is no longer in America.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.000
There are people who give charity, and so on.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:03.000
But, now, I read in a magazine, just this morning, I read in a magazine, that Israel is now sending money to Hosea Al-Anas.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.000
For education, and so on.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:14.000
Israel is sending money to Hosea Al-Anas to prevent assimilation in Israel.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.000
I mean, in a few seconds.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Let me tell you what I want to do this morning.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.000
We studied the Sufyan last week.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:29.000
And, it's such a key Sufyan, and we didn't finish it.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
But, I think I want to go over the whole Sufyan again.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.000
And, because it deals with basic ideas.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
All right?

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.000
And, let's see, first of all, it's Lamed Hea Amud-Bed.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Rabbi Haneva Papa Rameh.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.000
All right.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:52.000
Before I...

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
Let me hear something.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Rabbi Haneva Papa Rameh.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Rabbi Haneva Papa Rameh.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.000
All right.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.000
Let me just explain.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.000
I'm sorry.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.000
The sequence of subjects.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:14.000
Because, we want to say Berachah, or we say Berachah, and we want to find a biblical source.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.000
We don't have it.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:22.000
If we don't have a biblical source, then we develop a concept.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:29.000
And, the concept is, the earth is the Lord.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.000
It's the Lord's.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.000
The earth belongs to God.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:43.000
Therefore, if the earth belongs to God, before you take advantage or benefit from anything produced by the earth,

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:47.000
you should acknowledge that he is the master of the world.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.000
That's a beautiful concept.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.000
And, for the concept, for that concept, you have already a basuk.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.000
What's the basuk?

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.000
One basuk says, ladonai ha-ares yohah.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:05.000
The earth and all of its content belong to the Lord.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:12.000
The other basuk says, al-shamai, shamai ladonai, mea ares hatani mea haram.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.000
The earth is yours.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.000
So, there's a contradiction.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:19.000
No contradiction.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Kani b'ne Berachah, kani ha-gera.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:27.000
When you say Berachah, the earth is the Lord's.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.000
After Berachah, the earth is given to you.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Simple idea.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.000
So, yad-ia is a very interesting thing.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:44.000
First of all, I want to show you something very important about yad-ia.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:49.000
The mental attitude underlying this kind of reasoning.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.000
You have one basuk.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Ladonai ha-ares yohah.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
The earth belongs to God.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.000
Another basuk.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.000
Mea ares hatani mea haram.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.000
It should.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.000
So, instead of seeing it as a contradiction,

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.000
you must build a theory

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:15.000
in which you can fit those blocks.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:19.000
And the theory is Berachah.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.000
Understand?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.000
It's a very important thing.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.000
The attitude.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.000
Today they have a competition.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.000
You find one basuk.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.000
You say, oh, that's a mistake.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.000
The people are critics.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.000
That's a mistake.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.000
That's this.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.000
That's that.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.000
Well, they don't understand how the human mind works.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.000
This, instead of saying this is a mistake,

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.000
is totally negative.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.000
You say, no.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.000
There may be a theory behind it.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.000
Let's see if we can build a theory

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:53.000
in which those so-called opposite elements,

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.000
ladonai ha-ares yohah,

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.000
mea ares hatani mea haram,

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:04.000
could be somehow made to fit.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.000
So, but that is the background.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:12.000
Now, on the basis of this background,

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.000
I'm going to say something else.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.000
I'm going to extend it.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:22.000
Well, if the whole earth belongs to God,

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:29.000
then what is my function as an individual

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.000
in working and this and that?

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Well, I thought before this dersha

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.000
that when I work,

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.000
that this earth belongs to me.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.000
It's mine.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.000
I don't need a dersha.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.000
I work.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.000
I toil.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.000
And therefore, because I toil,

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.000
I got something.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:53.000
My grapes are flourishing.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.000
My grain is ripe and so on.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.000
So I always thought

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:02.000
that this had to do with my individual work.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.000
The earth is mine.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.000
I work.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:09.000
And therefore, it doesn't depend on God.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.000
It's individual work.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.000
So in a sense,

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.000
this opens a difficult problem to resolve.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:22.000
What is my function if the earth belongs to God?

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.000
And if it gives it,

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:29.000
then what is the function of work?

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.000
Does it make any difference whether I'm working

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.000
at 5 o'clock in the morning

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
or 4 o'clock in the morning

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.000
or 7 o'clock in the morning?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Does it make any difference?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.000
There is still a question.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.000
So because of this,

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.000
now we're going to analyze.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.000
And this is the thing.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.000
So as an introduction,

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.000
before we...

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.000
The most important things,

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.000
of course, were the Torah,

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.000
is what the Tana'im said.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.000
But sometimes,

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
before we reach,

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.000
before we study this Tana'imic source,

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:05.000
they give us an introduction.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.000
The introduction is going to be from the Emoraim.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.000
The purpose of it is

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.000
to serve as a bridge

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.000
for us to be able to

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.000
properly understand, properly decode

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.000
the Baraitan.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.000
So there is a Baraitan.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.000
But for the Baraitan,

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.000
we're going to see

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.000
what is the Emoraitic teaching,

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.000
which, of course, the editors

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.000
bring here

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.000
to serve as a kind of a bridge.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.000
Yes?

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.000
Let's say...

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.000
Yes.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.000
The etzyn is the last syllable.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.000
Now,

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.000
in the book of Hosea,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.000
there is the metaphor.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.000
The first target of the metaphor

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.000
of Israel as the wife of God

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.000
is in the book of Hosea.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.000
Israel is the wife of God.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.000
God, as a husband,

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.000
is duly bound

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.000
to support, physically,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.000
his wife.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.000
Now, all of a sudden

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.000
he's angry at us because we're worshipping idols.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.000
We're worshipping idols.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.000
God says...

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.000
You go to work, work, work,

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.000
and at the moment

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.000
that you're supposed to write it,

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.000
to harvest it,

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.000
at the moment I got up,

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.000
I'm going to take it easy.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.000
I'm going to make you work,

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.000
and then the person

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.000
will not be able to wipe

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.000
the fruits.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.000
It's a curse.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.000
But it's interesting there.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.000
It says, I believe,

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.000
no question about it in my mind,

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.000
that Hosea had the pasuk,

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.000
...

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.000
...

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.000
I was going to kill the rain.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.000
...

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.000
...

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
Now, Hosea had this

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.000
pasuk, place,

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.000
...

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.000
...

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.000
...

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.000
The question is like this.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.000
I work for it.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.000
It's my land.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.000
What should be the

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.000
...

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.000
...

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.000
It's not.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.000
...

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.000
...

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.000
...

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.000
What does it mean?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.000
...

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.000
...

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.000
...

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.000
...

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.000
Now it's interesting.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.000
When you harvest it,

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.000
it's yours.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.000
...

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.000
He takes it away before he harvests it.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.000
...

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.000
So is it the gun of God,

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.000
or is the gun of man?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.000
...

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.000
It's a theological

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.000
problem here.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.000
...

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.000
...

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.000
...

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.000
...

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.000
...

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.000
Yes.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
No.

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:39.000
There is no such thing that God gives you,

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.000
or belongs to you.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.000
It depends.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.000
There is a partnership, yes,

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.000
between God and

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.000
Israel.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.000
If we do our duties,

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.000
then God

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.000
will let us

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.000
that it will be our

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.000
...

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.000
But if we don't do our responsibilities,

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.000
then God is going

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.000
to withdraw that which

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.000
is supposed to be

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.000
ours. In other words, here

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.000
comes the very beautiful simile

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:13.000
of Hosea.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.000
... is like the husband

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.000
of Israel. Yes.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.000
If the wife

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.000
does

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
her responsibility,

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
